# Rank 1532 / CVE-2026-44213: OpenTelemetry .NET's Instana exporter
# disabled TLS certificate validation wholesale whenever a proxy was
# configured through INSTANA_ENDPOINT_PROXY, so a network attacker
# who could man-in-the-middle the proxy connection received all
# telemetry and the Instana API key (improper certificate validation,
# CWE-295; GHSA-wfr5-454p-mjc2, fixed in 1.1.0; the task list's
# nocommit flag was advisory-side absence -- the changelog's 1.1.0
# entry names PR #4153, which IS pool commit 3b5b6e1405). Configure
# in src/OpenTelemetry.Exporter.Instana/Implementation/Transport.cs
# did `if (Uri.TryCreate(proxy, UriKind.Absolute, out var
# proxyAddress)) { configuredHandler.Proxy = new WebProxy(
# proxyAddress, true); configuredHandler.UseProxy = true;
# configuredHandler.ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback =
# delegate { return true; }; }` -- an unconditional acceptance
# callback attached to the proxy branch. The fix removes the bypass
# from the production path (validation defaults stay on; the
# HttpClientFactory option lets callers take responsibility
# explicitly).
#
# FIXED, delegate-form binding shipped. The corpus already had two
# CertValidationDisabled bindings (VYQL-CFG-004) -- one anchored on
# DangerousAcceptAnyServerCertificateValidator, one on a
# ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback CALL carrying literal
# true -- but the assignment form `... = delegate { return true; }`
# matched neither. This adds certValidationDisabledDelegate to
# vyql/bindings/csharp/m1caa8bf2.vyql: a presence rule on functions
# whose callPath mentions ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback
# and whose literals contain true, excluding functions whose name
# mentions Validate. Measured: the vulnerable Transport.cs at the
# fix parent now reports VYQL-CFG-004 HIGH, the fix revision reports
# zero, and two legitimate shapes stay silent -- a named validator
# method assignment (h.ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback =
# ValidateCertificate, whose body's return true sits in a function
# named Validate) and a conditional lambda ((msg, cert, chain,
# errors) => errors == SslPolicyErrors.None). No
# ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback exists anywhere in the
# benchmark corpora, and the full suite plus both benchmarks pass
# below. Spec cve_rank1532 records the proxy-branch bypass expecting
# VYQL-CFG-004 and the factory-configured form rejecting it.

test "rank1532: the proxy branch accepts any certificate"
  lang csharp
  file src/OpenTelemetry.Exporter.Instana/Implementation/Transport.cs
  expect VYQL-CFG-004
  code
  ```
  using System;
  using System.Net;

  public class Transport
  {
      public static HttpClientHandler ConfigureHandler(HttpClientHandler configuredHandler)
      {
          var proxy = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("INSTANA_ENDPOINT_PROXY");
          if (Uri.TryCreate(proxy, UriKind.Absolute, out var proxyAddress))
          {
              configuredHandler.Proxy = new WebProxy(proxyAddress, true);
              configuredHandler.UseProxy = true;
              configuredHandler.ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback = delegate { return true; };
          }
          return configuredHandler;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1532: the fix leaves validation on by default"
  lang csharp
  file src/OpenTelemetry.Exporter.Instana/Implementation/Transport.cs
  reject VYQL-CFG-004
  code
  ```
  using System;
  using System.Net;

  public class Transport
  {
      public static HttpClientHandler ConfigureHandler(HttpClientHandler configuredHandler)
      {
          var proxy = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("INSTANA_ENDPOINT_PROXY");
          if (Uri.TryCreate(proxy, UriKind.Absolute, out var proxyAddress))
          {
              configuredHandler.Proxy = new WebProxy(proxyAddress, true);
              configuredHandler.UseProxy = true;
          }
          return configuredHandler;
      }
  }
  ```
